{"user": "I\u2019m Black in this Othello endgame. My legal moves are g2, b6, a7, b7, b8, c8. Which one maximizes my final disc count against optimal White play? Could you quickly evaluate the critical lines?", "user_ts": "2026-08-04T19:00:57.451380+00:00", "assistant": "**Best move: b7.**\n\nWhy it\u2019s critical:\n\n- **b7 flips g7 to Black**, which shuts off White\u2019s immediate **a1 corner** access along the diagonal a1\u2013b2\u2013c3\u2013d4\u2013e5\u2013f6\u2013g7.\n- If Black plays almost anything else (**g2, b6, a7, b8, c8**), White can answer **a1**, taking a permanent corner and Black can\u2019t fully recover with optimal play.\n- Although **c8 flips the most discs immediately**, it still leaves **g7 White**, so White\u2019s **a1** corner reply is the key refutation.\n\nAfter **1. b7**, White\u2019s main tries are around **b6 / c8 / a3**, but none restore that immediate corner threat without giving Black compensation. So the maximizing move is:\n\n**1. b7**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-04T19:00:57.451380+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-04T19:01:02.451380+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Common Ground Question": 1, "Solution Request": 2}, "confidence": {"Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333, "Solution Request": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line"], "consensus": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line"], "votes": {"Move Verdict": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 2, "General Principle": 1}, "confidence": {"Move Verdict": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 0.6666666666666666, "General Principle": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Move Verdic