{"user": "Follow-up: after 1. b7 White can play b6 and flip several discs on the b-file. Does Black still have a clear path to outcount White, or do lines get messy?", "user_ts": "2026-08-04T19:01:12.451380+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 **White 1...b6 is the critical try, but Black still has a clear winning path**.\n\nKey line:\n\n**1. b7 b6 2. c8!**\n\nNot **2. a1?** \u2014 that\u2019s too slow. **c8** takes control of the bottom edge and creates strong mobility threats.\n\nWhite\u2019s best resistance is:\n\n**2...a8 3. a3! 4. b8 g2 5. h1 a1**, White has no useful move, then Black finishes with **a7**.\n\nSo the line is roughly:\n\n**b7, b6, c8, a8, a3, b8, g2, h1, a1, pass, a7**\n\nBlack finishes ahead, about **35\u201329**.  \nSo: **b6 makes it look messy, but c8 keeps it under control.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-04T19:01:12.451380+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-04T19:01:17.451380+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Common Ground Question": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Move Verdict", "Board Report", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "Neutral Feedback"], "consensus": ["Move Verdict", "Board Report", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "Neutral Feedback"], "votes": {"Move Verdict": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 3, "Positive Feedback": 1, "Neutral Feedback": 2, "Board Report": 2, "Negative Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Move Verdict": 1.0, "Local Justificatio